  "selectionGuide": {
    "brief": "방어 · 섬멸 — 편성 1+4+9 = 14명",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "rule",
        "text": "ARCHETYPES: SECURITY, SEEK & DESTROY"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "OPERATIVES"
      },
      {
        "type": "rule",
        "text": "↘ 1 DEATH KORPS WATCHMASTER operative with the following:\n• Boltgun; bayonet\nOr one option from each of the following:\n• Bolt pistol, plasma pistol or relic laspistol\n• Chainsword or power weapon"
      },
      {
        "type": "rule",
        "text": "↘ 4 TROOPER operatives"
      },
      {
        "type": "rule",
        "text": "↘ 9 DEATH KORPS operatives selected from the following list:\n• BRUISER\n• CONFIDANT with one of the following options:\n○ Boltgun or lasgun; bayonet\n○ Bolt pistol or relic laspistol; chainsword\n• GUNNER with bayonet and flamer\n• GUNNER with bayonet and grenade launcher"
      },
      {
        "type": "rule",
        "text": "• GUNNER with bayonet and meltagun\n• GUNNER with bayonet and plasma gun\n• MEDIC\n• SAPPER\n• SNIPER\n• SPOTTER\n• TROOPER\n• VETERAN\n• VOX-OPERATOR\n• ZEALOT"
      },
      {
        "type": "rule",
        "text": "Other than TROOPER operatives, your kill team can only include each operative on this list once. Up to four times, instead of selecting one of these TROOPER operatives, you can select one DEATH KORPS ploy to cost you 0CP for the battle."
      }
    ]
  },
  "factionRule": {
    "brief": "GUARDSMEN ORDERS · Take Aim! · Fix Bayonets! …",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "GUARDSMEN ORDERS"
      },
      {
        "type": "lore",
        "text": "The soldiers of the Death Korps of Krieg are unquestioningly loyal to their officers, following barked orders with a speed and efficiency that is the envy of many other regiments."
      },
      {
        "type": "rule",
        "text": "STRATEGIC GAMBIT and SUPPORT. A friendly DEATH KORPS WATCHMASTER operative can issue a GUARDSMAN ORDER. Whenever it does, select one GUARDSMAN ORDER for all friendly DEATH KORPS operatives within 6\" of it to receive. Whenever a friendly operative receives a GUARDSMAN ORDER, apply its rules until the end of the turning point. Operatives cannot benefit from more than one GUARDSMAN ORDER at once; they only benefit from the most recent order they received during the turning point."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "GUARDSMEN ORDERS OPTIONS ARE"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "PRESENTED ON THEIR OWN CARDS"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "GUARDSMEN ORDERS"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Take Aim!"
      },
      {
        "type": "lore",
        "text": "Outfitted and trained for attritional infantry combat, the soldiers of Krieg have undertaken endless hours of lasgun drills."
      },
      {
        "type": "rule",
        "text": "Ranged weapons of operatives that received this order (excluding mortar barrage and remote detonator) have the Ceaseless weapon rule."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Fix Bayonets!"
      },
      {
        "type": "lore",
        "text": "The kind of warfare undertaken by the Death Korps of Krieg requires their troopers to be well versed in close-quarters fighting and trench clearance."
      },
      {
        "type": "rule",
        "text": "Melee weapons of operatives that received this order have the Ceaseless weapon rule."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "GUARDSMEN ORDERS"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Dig In!"
      },
      {
        "type": "lore",
        "text": "Obstinate to the last, the soldiers of Krieg establish defensive positions and hold them with grim determination."
      },
      {
        "type": "rule",
        "text": "Whenever an operative is shooting a friendly operative that's received this order, if you can retain any cover saves, you can re-roll any of your defence dice results of one result (e.g. results of 2)."
      },
      {
        "type": "lore",
        "text": "Move! Move! Move! Responding to a barked order from their Watchmaster, the soldiers of Krieg pick up the pace and hustle towards their next objective."
      },
      {
        "type": "rule",
        "text": "Whenever an operative that's received this order is performing the Reposition action, add 1\" to its Move stat."
      }
    ]
  },
  "source": "공식 Kill Team 앱 PDF 추출본"
}
